From: PwndaWallet swap sidecar
Date: 2026-09-03
Subject: [PATCH 17/19] basicswap: guard ZanoInterface's main-wallet-rpc calls
 against sending from the wrong wallet, mirroring PWNDA-PATCH-8's xmr.py
 assertion

PWNDA-PATCH-8's xmr.py hunk added a wrong-wallet assertion to
XMRInterface.publishBLockTx, immediately before the transfer call --
the same shape upstream commit 10ee0843 already gave findTxB and
spendBLockTx ("guard against wrong-wallet reads made possible due to
the preceding optimization commit"). Under Grove's host-managed-main-
wallet deployment (PWNDA-PATCH-5 for XMR, PWNDA-PATCH-15's
_external_main_wallet for ZANO), the host independently owns the
wallet-rpc process this connection talks to and can switch or replace
its account between the moment this interface last confirmed its
identity and the moment it sends funds through it. PWNDA-PATCH-15
(0015-zano-coin-module.patch) built the _external_main_wallet flag and
the initialiseWallet no-op that makes host-wallet sharing possible for
ZANO, but did not yet add a guard on the calls in ZanoInterface that
actually move funds -- this patch is that guard.

ZanoInterface cannot reuse xmr.py's exact mechanism verbatim: it does
not inherit XMRInterface (it inherits CoinInterface directly -- see
0015's class ZanoInterface(CoinInterface)), and Zano's wallet-rpc has
no open_wallet/close_wallet RPC at all (ZanoInterface.openWallet is
already a documented no-op -- Zano's wallet-rpc process always serves
whatever account it was started with or last had generate_from_keys
run against it). XMRInterface's _cached_main_wallet_address is
populated by openWallet()'s fast path, which runs at the top of every
wallet-touching call including publishBLockTx itself; ZanoInterface
has no equivalent hook to populate it from.

REVISED 2026-09-03 (Grove expansion master plan Verify phase): the
first version of this patch guarded publishBLockTx alone. A 3-reviewer
adversarial verify pass on unit B-X3's own output caught that
ZanoInterface.withdrawCoin makes two of its own
rpc_wallet("transfer", ...) calls on the SAME host-managed connection
(the sweep-all branch and the plain-withdraw branch) with no identity
check at all -- and withdrawCoin is reachable via the webview UI and
the JSON-RPC `withdraw` route, not only from the swap engine. The
patch's own header and an inline comment claimed publishBLockTx was
"the one/single fund-moving main-wallet call in ZanoInterface", which
was false: PWNDA-PATCH-15's own inline comment on the two-wallet-split
rationale had already named withdrawCoin alongside publishBLockTx as a
call that "would then silently operate on the wrong account" -- the
pointer was sitting in the file this patch edits and was not followed
the first time. See PwndaWalletVault/log.md's 2026-09-03 "PATCH-17
coverage gap" entry for the full finding and this fix's verification.

Four changes, all in basicswap/interface/zano/zano.py (0015's new
file -- no shared-file conflict):

1. __init__: adds self._cached_main_wallet_address, same name and
   role as XMRInterface's field, initialised to None.

2. initialiseWallet's _external_main_wallet branch (0015's Grove-only
   no-op path): after logging, confirms and caches the live wallet's
   address via a getaddress call. This is ZANO's analogue of
   PWNDA-PATCH-8's basicswap.py checkWalletSeed hunk for XMR -- the
   "host confirms its wallet's identity" moment, which for ZANO
   happens here (bin/prepare.py's provisioning loop / reseedWallet, per
   0015's own comment on this method) rather than in checkWalletSeed
   (basicswap.py's xmr_based_coins branch does not special-case ZANO
   today; when B-X2/0016 registers ZANO into that list, this cache is
   additional defence, not required by it). A failed read leaves the
   cache at None rather than a stale or guessed value.

3. A new shared method, _confirmMainWalletIdentity: re-reads the
   connection's live address and compares it to the cached value from
   (2). Any mismatch -- INCLUDING "nothing was ever cached" (None) --
   raises TemporaryError before the caller's fund-moving call is
   reached. Fails closed deliberately: an unconfirmed wallet is not
   treated as an acceptable one to spend from. Gated on
   self._external_main_wallet, exactly as PATCH-8's xmr.py guard is
   gated on the equivalent XMR flag, so a non-Grove embedder running
   0015 with _external_main_wallet left at its default (False) sees no
   behaviour change from this patch at all. Factored out as its own
   method (rather than inlined per call site, as the first version of
   this patch did) specifically so a future fund-moving call added to
   this file only has to call it, not reimplement it.

4. Three call sites, all immediately before their own
   self.rpc_wallet("transfer", ...) call: publishBLockTx (the swap
   settlement leg, as before), and withdrawCoin's two branches
   (sweep-all and plain transfer, newly guarded).

Deliberately NOT done here (out of scope for this unit, no shared-file
edits): registering ZANO into basicswap.py's xmr_based_coins /
checkWalletSeed special case (that is PWNDA-PATCH-16 / B-X2's and the
integrator's business, and this guard does not depend on it -- the
cache is populated locally, inside zano.py, by (2) above, independent
of whether the shared checkWalletSeed hunk ever sees Coins.ZANO).

Verification: py_compile against a scratch copy at p12+0015 (0013 also
present as a harmless, file-disjoint extra -- new zephyr module only);
a hand-built mutation test with a stubbed rpc_wallet confirms
_confirmMainWalletIdentity raises TemporaryError before any of the
three callers' "transfer" stub branch is ever reached, for a
live-address mismatch and for an unconfirmed (None) cache, on ALL
THREE call sites (publishBLockTx, withdrawCoin sweep-all,
withdrawCoin plain) -- not just the one the first version tested --
plus a positive control confirming a matching identity does not block
a legitimate send. See PwndaWalletVault/log.md's 2026-09-03 entries
("Unit B-X3: Zano host-wallet guard" and the same-day "PATCH-17
coverage gap" follow-up) and
PwndaWalletVault/wiki/synthesis/grove-expansion-master-plan.md (§ 3,
unit B-X3) for the full writeup.

